import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 697 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
rows = [
"| 698 | 2026-10-27 | **Counting her way: the bottom number names the note that is one beat (Build BF; her 15:04).** 8 on the bottom: the quaver is one beat and every note counts double (crotchet 2, dotted crotchet 3, dotted minim 6); 2 on the bottom: the minim is one beat and every note counts half. The time-signatures chapter already taught this (BeatDoubler, The bottom number changes the beat); the 6/8 chapter (Build AD) and the later rhythm rooms had drifted to 'two big beats'. Now: 6/8 step 1 is The quaver is one beat and opens with that toy (4 or 8 on the bottom), the printed page shows the five notes with their beats doubled; the dotted crotchet is 3 beats, the crotchet 2; the minim beat step (Rhythm Further) opens with the toy (4 or 2); 9/8 nine beats in threes, 12/8 twelve, 6/4 six; 'big beat' is gone from every student screen, the Workbook and the teacher's copies; the exam's names (compound duple and the like) stay only where a theory step names time signatures; the time-signature drill's level 9 is Compound time: groups of three; the 6/8 drill's level 2 is How many beats?. Source patch725.py; test bf725.js. |",
"| 699 | 2026-10-27 | **One bar, two bars, then all four by ear (Build BG; her 15:04).** Every clap-back pad in a Lesson Book (Listen, Clap, Write; Hear and Sing Further; Hear and Sing, Grades 4 and 5) starts with one bar: heard once, echoed at once, the notes shown (Grade 1 with walk and run-ning, 타 / 티, under them; a minim 'hold'), then two bars, then all four as the test is (heard twice, then two or three). The notes can be hidden; after a try at all four, the bars that went wrong are offered again one by one. The longer tune of Hear and Sing Further: the first half, the second half, then the whole tune. The drills and the Home lessons stay as the test is. Source patch726.py; test bg726.js. |",
"| 700 | 2026-10-27 | **Blues jam (Build BH; her 15:04, 'the blues and making things up were fun').** A 12-bar blues band in C loops (the Styles room's swung boogie without its ending); only the C blues scale plays (C, E♭, F, F♯, G, B♭), three notes first, then all six; the bar now playing lights on the 12-bar chart; every note is kept and Hear my solo plays it back over the band. In the Styles room's Blues step after Blues and swing, in the Toolbox and in the Styles room on the Home. Source patch727.py; test bh727.js. chsweep 46 chapters 0 errors, booksweep 0 errors, regression 323 lessons, 54 drills, 0 errors. Local commit only, not pushed. |",
]
for r in reversed(rows): lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, r)
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
